// ============================================================================
//  mod_revise.zone  -  assets found MISSING by .agents\audit_weapon_assets.js.
//
//  Written 2026-08-16 (v1.99.14) on the user's "revise" instruction: go over the
//  whole mod and check that everything added is integrated properly and is not
//  missing effects.
//
//  🌟 HOW THESE WERE FOUND. The audit enumerates every asset a weapon def names
//  BY VALUE - not by field-name pattern - and resolves each one against
//  (a) what mod.ff declares and (b) the fastfiles each zombies map actually
//  loads, taken from the "Loading fastfile" lines of a real console_zm.log.
//  Anything in neither is a SILENT failure in T6: no log line, no error, just a
//  missing effect or a bind-pose model.
//
//  The bug that prompted the tool: the Tac-45's five left-hand dual-wield anims
//  were referenced and declared nowhere, so the Pack-a-Punched gun drew at bind
//  pose - an enormous misplaced model. See mod_tac45.zone.
// ============================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  1. THE KILL-FEED / HUD ICONS FOR TEN PORTED WEAPONS.
//
//  🌟 This is the README's long-standing "Kill-feed icons missing" known issue,
//  and this is its cause. Every ported MP weapon names a hudIcon / killIcon /
//  ammoCounterIcon material, and for ten of the twelve that material ships ONLY
//  in code_post_gfx_mp.ff and frontend.ff - neither of which a zombies map
//  loads. So the icon resolved to nothing and the feed drew a blank.
//
//  The XPR-50, the Titus-6 and the Tac-45 were already correct: menu_mp_weapons_as50,
//  menu_mp_weapons_titus and menu_mp_weapons_fnp45 are declared in their own
//  zone files. These ten complete the set.
//
//  📝 Names are the defs' own values, read out of each weapon file - note
//  peacekeeper uses `_pm` and vector uses `_kriss`, both development names.
//  code_post_gfx_mp.ff is already in build_ff.bat's --load list, so no load-order
//  change and no new fastfile.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
material,menu_mp_weapons_sig556
material,menu_mp_weapons_sa58
material,menu_mp_weapons_mk48
material,menu_mp_weapons_qbb95
material,menu_mp_weapons_mp7
material,menu_mp_weapons_kriss
material,menu_mp_weapons_insas
material,menu_mp_weapons_pm
material,menu_mp_weapons_crossbow

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  2. THE WINTER'S HOWL'S PROJECTILE TRAIL MATERIAL.
//
//  🌟 The gun is weaponType `projectile` with projectileSpeed 2000 and had NO
//  projTrailEffect at all - so it fired an invisible projectile. The Wunderwaffe,
//  which the user is happy with, has both projTrailEffect and projExplosionEffect.
//  The mod has shipped fx_trail_freezegun_geotail and fx_trail_freezegun_ring_emit
//  since the port went in; both are declared, both load (console_zm.log:4469-4470)
//  and NOTHING referenced either of them. geotail's `emission` field names
//  ring_emit, so the two are one trail.
//
//  Of the six materials that trail needs, five already resolve:
//        gfx_fxt_light_flare                 already in mod.ff
//        gfx_fxt_env_water_droplets_add      already in mod.ff
//        gfx_fxt_env_dust_mote_pcloud_2_add  already in mod.ff
//        gfx_fxt_muz_vert_gen                common_zm  (every map)
//        gfx_fxt_smk_puff                    common_zm  (every map)
//  The sixth - the main wisp of the trail - ships only in zm_highrise, zm_nuked,
//  zm_tomb and the two so_zclassic zones. It is ABSENT on zm_transit, which is
//  the map this is tested on, so it has to come with the mod.
//  zm_highrise.ff is already --load'ed.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
image,fxt_smk_trail_wisp
material,gfx_fxt_smk_trail_wisp

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  3. THE TITUS-6'S DIVE-TO-PRONE ANIMATIONS, BOTH FIRE MODES.
//
//  Referenced by titus6_zm / titus6_upgraded_zm (dtp_in/loop/out) and by
//  mk_titus6_zm / mk_titus6_upgraded_zm, declared nowhere. Diving to prone with
//  the Titus in hand would have dropped the viewmodel to bind pose - the same
//  class of defect as the Tac-45's left hand, just on a rarer input.
//  All six are in monsoon.ff, already --load'ed for this weapon.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
xanim,viewmodel_titus_gl_d2p_in
xanim,viewmodel_titus_gl_d2p_loop
xanim,viewmodel_titus_gl_d2p_out
xanim,viewmodel_titus_mk_d2p_in
xanim,viewmodel_titus_mk_d2p_loop
xanim,viewmodel_titus_mk_d2p_out

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  4. SHELL EJECT AND MUZZLE EFFECTS THAT ARE NOT ON EVERY MAP.
//
//  fx_saw          - the Mk 48 / QBB LSW shell eject. On every zombies map
//                    EXCEPT zm_prison, so belt-fed brass vanished on Mob.
//                    From common_mp.ff.
//  fx_zombie_heavy_flash_base_ug - the XPR-50's Pack-a-Punched muzzle flash.
//                    On every map except zm_tomb, so the packed XPR-50 fired
//                    with no flash on Origins. From zm_buried.ff.
//  reticle_center_cross_glow - the Titus-6 dart's reticle. Only in zm_prison
//                    and common.ff of the zones this build loads.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
fx,weapon/shellejects/fx_saw
fx,weapon/muzzleflashes/fx_zombie_heavy_flash_base_ug
material,reticle_center_cross_glow
